# Copy the required variable names into the host's environment settings.
# This reference intentionally contains no values or credentials.

# Runtime
# NODE_ENV — Set to production on the hosted service.
# PORT — Listening port; supplied automatically by the host.
# FRONTEND_URL — Main browser origin allowed by Express and Socket.IO CORS.
# APP_URL — Additional browser origin allowed by Express CORS.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS — Optional comma-separated additional CORS origins.

# Security and authentication
# JWT_SECRET — Long random signing key; required in production.
# SESSION_EXPIRY_DAYS — JWT lifetime in days.
# BCRYPT_SALT_ROUNDS — Password hashing work factor.

# Database
# DATABASE_URL — PostgreSQL connection string used by the running app.
# DIRECT_URL — Direct PostgreSQL connection string used by Prisma CLI schema commands.

# OTP
# OTP_EXPIRY_MINUTES — OTP validity period.
# OTP_LENGTH — Number of digits in generated OTPs.
# OTP_MAX_ATTEMPTS — Maximum verification attempts per OTP.
# OTP_RESEND_COOLDOWN_SECONDS — Minimum interval between OTP sends.
# OTP_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_HOUR — Maximum OTP sends per user per hour.
# DEV_OTP_MODE — Development-only OTP behavior; disabled automatically in production.

# Email (optional; provider defaults to mock)
# EMAIL_PROVIDER — Email provider selection.
# EMAIL_HOST — SMTP host.
# EMAIL_PORT — SMTP port.
# EMAIL_USER — SMTP username.
# EMAIL_PASSWORD — SMTP password or app password.
# EMAIL_FROM — Sender name and address.

# WhatsApp (optional; configure credentials for the selected provider)
# WHATSAPP_PROVIDER — WhatsApp provider selection.
# WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN — Meta WhatsApp API access token.
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID — Meta WhatsApp phone number ID.
# WHATSAPP_BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID — Meta WhatsApp business account ID.
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID — Twilio account SID.
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN — Twilio auth token.
# TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM — Twilio WhatsApp sender.
# TWILIO_CONTENT_SID — Optional approved Twilio content template SID.

# Other integrations (optional)
# GEMINI_API_KEY — Google Gemini API key.
# NAMASTEQR_PRINTER_ALLOWED_HOSTS — Optional comma-separated explicit printer relay hosts.
# NAMASTEQR_PRINTER_ALLOWED_PORTS — Optional comma-separated explicit printer relay ports.

# Development / helper processes (optional; not needed by the Render web service)
# DISABLE_HMR — Disable Vite hot module replacement when set to true.
# VITE_DEV — Force the development Vite middleware path when set.
# BRIDGE_PORT — Local printer bridge listen port.
# PRINTER_HOST — Local printer host for the standalone bridge script.
# PRINTER_PORT — Local printer port for the standalone bridge script.
# PRINT_AGENT_CONFIG — Path to the standalone restaurant print agent JSON config.
